<title>PHILIPPINES: JAPAN JGC, NIKFILL TO BUILD MANILA PETROCHEM PLANT.</title>
<headline>JAPAN JGC, NIKFILL TO BUILD MANILA PETROCHEM PLANT.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two Japanese companies have been awarded contracts to build the Philippines' first polyethylene plant, Bataan Polyethylene Corp (BPC) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>BPC said in a statement it had given the engineering and procurement contract to JGC Corporation, while the actual construction will be done by Nikfill Construction Co Inc.</p>
<p>The company did not give the project cost for the plant which will produce 250,000 tonnes of polyethylene per year.</p>
<p>The plant is expected to be operational by year 1999.</p>
<p>BPC is a joint venture among Bataan Polyethylene Holdings of the Philippines, British Petroleum, Petronas, and Sumitomo Corp.</p>
